PROJECT: After Hours Podcast — Podcast Landing & Guest Application Site

TECH STACK:
- React + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS
- Bolt Cloud PostgreSQL database (Supabase under the hood, managed by Bolt)
- React Router DOM for routing (/, /apply, /application, /privacy, /admin)
- n8n webhook for submission notifications
- AWS Lambda for admin authentication

DESIGN RULES (NEVER DEVIATE):
- Dark theme ONLY. Background: #0A0A0A. No light mode.
- Text: #FFFFFF for headings, #E5E5E5 for body, #999999 for muted/placeholder text
- Display font: "Bebas Neue" (Google Fonts) — ALL section headings, always uppercase, massive sizes (4xl–7xl responsive)
- Body font: Inter (or system sans-serif fallback)
- Accent: Warm amber neon gradient via class "text-gradient-gold" — linear-gradient(135deg, #F5C45E, #FFD98E)
- Primary amber hex: #F5C45E — used for text accents, icon strokes, borders, focus states
- Light amber hex: #FFD98E — used in gradients alongside primary
- RGBA amber: rgba(245, 196, 94, ...) — used for glows, shadows, transparent backgrounds
- Every H2 follows the pattern: white text + LAST WORD wrapped in <span className="text-gradient-gold">
- Section separators: border-t with subtle amber glow (border-gold-glow class)
- CTA buttons: btn-gold class (amber gradient background, black text, rounded-xl, all caps)
- Cards: bg-[#0D0D0F], border-gold-glow, rounded-2xl, hover effects
- No nav bar on the landing page
- Max content width: 1200px for landing sections, 640px for application form

EXISTING FUNCTIONALITY (DO NOT BREAK):
- Homepage (LandingPage.tsx) with scroll animations and animated stat counters
- /apply sales page (ApplyPage.tsx) with scroll animations
- /application form (ApplicationPage.tsx) → Supabase applications table + n8n webhook
- Admin dashboard at /admin with Lambda auth
- Privacy Policy at /privacy
- useScrollReveal hook for animations

